  "conclusions": [
    "Fabric and Forge both copy inbound bytes before scheduling, bound 30000 bytes, and recheck exact live connection/listener ownership on the main thread and on asynchronous report responses.",
    "Forge PLAY_TO_SERVER=ClientCustomPayloadEvent and PLAY_TO_CLIENT=ServerCustomPayloadEvent match official Forge37; explicit direction checks exclude LOGIN subclasses.",
    "Forge client-only class has Dist.CLIENT metadata; official AutomaticEventSubscriber filters physical side before Class.forName. Common entry/bridge has no net.minecraft.client reference.",
    "Required Commands.performCommand(CommandSourceStack,String):int HEAD gate matches official 1.17.1 mappings; pending actual owner is checked before command execution, including OP commands.",
    "Both helpers use object identity, current transport listener, connected state and PLAY checks; the Fabric and Forge dispatcher implementations are identical apart from package.",
    "Fabric API distribution identifies as fabric, matching the new descriptor dependency. Both descriptors constrain Minecraft1.17.1, Java16/Forge37, GPL3-only; Forge Mixin0.8.4 officially defines JAVA_16."
  ],
